# Git Worktree & Task Tracking Protocols

## Worktrunk (`wt`) Isolation
- Never commit or modify files directly on the primary working tree or default branch (`main` / `master`).
- Always spawn a dedicated worktree using `wt switch --create <branch-name>`.
- Confine all file changes, subagents, and command executions strictly to the worktree path.

## Zero Untracked Work Protocol (`pm`)
- All work must be associated with an issue (`Issue #<N>`).
- Auto-create an issue using `gh issue create` if none exists before writing code.
- Prefix worktree branches with issue reference: `feature/<N>-<slug>` or `fix/<N>-<slug>`.
- Link PRs with `Fixes #<N>`.
- Keep issues open with `status:completed` until PR merge.
